  "foaf:name": "Morocco Ocean Climate Innovation Hub",
  "sdo:name": "Morocco Ocean Climate Innovation Hub",
  "sdo:description": "Morocco Ocean Climate Innovation Hub is a multi-actor platform designed to accelerate ocean–climate solutions in Africa and beyond. Anchored in Morocco as the Atlantic–Mediterranean bridge, it unites universities, foundations, youth networks, NGOs, startups, and policymakers within the global ecosystem of Ocean Climate Innovation Hubs. Its strategic triptych — sovereignty, ocean–climate literacy, and innovation -makes it unique: combining legal and governance tools, inclusive education (school to university), and incubation of blue startups. The Hub will strengthen Africa’s unified voice in international negotiations (CBD, UNFCCC, BBNJ, UNOC), while delivering practical solutions for adaptation, mitigation, and resilience. Built with a statutory structure and observatory, it is designed to endure beyond 2030, ensuring continuity of Africa’s leadership in ocean–climate governance.",
  "sdo:location": "Morocco",
  "sdo:identifier": "12.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/morocco-ocean-climate-innovation-hub/",
